{
  "abstract": "Let f(n) be the maximal number of edges of a graph on n vertices in which every cycle has more vertices than chords. Erdős Problem 642 (Hamburger and Szegedy) asks whether f(n) = O(n); this is open. This project proves the bound f(n) = O(n^(3/2)) attributed to Chen, Erdős and Staton, in the explicit form f(n) <= 2 (floor(sqrt n) + 1) n, by a longest path argument.",
